{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DwcZkgj99DzXM2JibHWsw7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Host contract\n2\t\n3\t`invoke(name, token, arguments, request_id)` is the only authenticated public\n4\tentrypoint. Hosts may choose the request ID; it has no authorization meaning.\n5\tThe session table maps opaque synthetic tokens to immutable identities. Callers\n6\tcontrol tool names and the complete arguments object, but not identity fields.\n7\t\n8\tAn unknown tool or inactive session is rejected before the handler executes.\n9\tHandlers return ordinary Python dictionaries or lists. Exceptions remain typed:\n10\tAccessDenied is a policy refusal, InvalidRequest is malformed input and NotFound\n11\tis a missing record. A host may translate these to transport errors unchanged.\n12\t\n13\tThe registry description is metadata, not an authorization decision. Tools must\n14\tperform their own permission checks. There is no wildcard tool or fallback route.\n15\tCompatibility manifest helpers are imported only by offline consumers and are not\n16\treachable through default registration. No supplied route evaluates record text.\n17\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5430cdda-5373-4192-a860-e85bfed12d9e","uuid":"e2f61a39-707b-4bfe-9cfc-a54aaf65e788","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:50:24.664Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"repo/docs/host-contract.md","content":"# Host contract\n\n`invoke(name, token, arguments, request_id)` is the only authenticated public\nentrypoint. Hosts may choose the request ID; it has no authorization meaning.\nThe session table maps opaque synthetic tokens to immutable identities. Callers\ncontrol tool names and the complete arguments object, but not identity fields.\n\nAn unknown tool or inactive session is rejected before the handler executes.\nHandlers return ordinary Python dictionaries or lists. Exceptions remain typed:\nAccessDenied is a policy refusal, InvalidRequest is malformed input and NotFound\nis a missing record. A host may translate these to transport errors unchanged.\n\nThe registry description is metadata, not an authorization decision. Tools must\nperform their own permission checks. There is no wildcard tool or fallback route.\nCompatibility manifest helpers are imported only by offline consumers and are not\nreachable through default registration. No supplied route evaluates record text.\n","numLines":17,"startLine":1,"totalLines":17}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DwcZkgj99DzXM2JibHWsw7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013Y4QMgUzAbzJQUGfwjmm6m","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Local operation\n2\t\n3\tThe source tree contains the entire request dispatcher. There is no HTTP server,\n4\treverse proxy, network ACL, database RLS, or external policy engine in this bundle.\n5\tThe MCP-shaped registry is called directly by a host adapter with a session token.\n6\tThe host adapter is assumed to forward the authenticated token and original object;\n7\tit does not authorize resource identifiers or rewrite arguments.\n8\t\n9\tUse `service.bootstrap.build()` with its default settings to obtain the registry.\n10\tThe returned tools are immediately callable via `Registry.invoke`. Startup imports\n11\tseed records into process memory. A restart resets all changes and audit events.\n12\tNo environment variables enable additional registration or change authorization.\n13\t\n14\tAudit events contain a subject, action, count and request ID. Record bodies and\n15\tsession tokens are not written to the audit queue. Queue overflow drops the oldest\n16\tevent. Operators must collect events before shutdown if retention is required.\n17\t\n18\tOnly the local profile is supplied. Production credential provisioning, network\n19\ttransport, persistence, log shipping, and rate limiting remain outside this sample.\n20\tThose unknown deployments must not be assumed to repair supplied access checks.\n21\tAll identities, tokens and records in the seed are synthetic demonstration data.\n22\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5430cdda-5373-4192-a860-e85bfed12d9e","uuid":"c2f622d4-376e-460a-8e7b-9232a518f097","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:50:24.668Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"repo/docs/operations.md","content":"# Local operation\n\nThe source tree contains the entire request dispatcher. There is no HTTP server,\nreverse proxy, network ACL, database RLS, or external policy engine in this bundle.\nThe MCP-shaped registry is called directly by a host adapter with a session token.\nThe host adapter is assumed to forward the authenticated token and original object;\nit does not authorize resource identifiers or rewrite arguments.\n\nUse `service.bootstrap.build()` with its default settings to obtain the registry.\nThe returned tools are immediately callable via `Registry.invoke`. Startup imports\nseed records into process memory. A restart resets all changes and audit events.\nNo environment variables enable additional registration or change authorization.\n\nAudit events contain a subject, action, count and request ID. Record bodies and\nsession tokens are not written to the audit queue. Queue overflow drops the oldest\nevent. Operators must collect events before shutdown if retention is required.\n\nOnly the local profile is supplied. Production credential provisioning, network\ntransport, persistence, log shipping, and rate limiting remain outside this sample.\nThose unknown deployments must not be assumed to repair supplied access checks.\nAll identities, tokens and records in the seed are synthetic demonstration data.\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013Y4QMgUzAbzJQUGfwjmm6m","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
